# StormTrack Pro: Build and Start Once When Fully Done

This is an Electron app (`npm run start` runs `electron .`). Every `npm run start` opens a new app window. Killing electron kills the user's running app. This is extremely disruptive.

## Rules (STRICT — no exceptions)

1. **Make ALL code edits first.** Do not build or start anything until every single file edit is done.
2. **Kill the running Electron process** as the very first deployment step: `taskkill /F /IM electron.exe 2>$null` (PowerShell).
3. **Build ONCE** after killing: run `npm run build` and wait for it to finish.
4. **Do NOT start the app.** The user will start it themselves with `npm run start`.
5. **NEVER run `npm run build` more than once per response.** One kill. One build. That's it.
6. **NEVER run build mid-response.** Only at the very end, after all edits are complete.

## Sequence (end of response only)

```
taskkill /F /IM electron.exe 2>$null   # kill old instance
npm run build                           # wait for completion
```
